course: dictionary
lesson: 10509
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word twin can name a person, describe a pair of matching things, or describe two towns that are partners. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «Isaac's son Jacob tricked his twin Esau» is about people, so twin means one of two children born to the same mother at the same time.
explain: In «twin beds», twin describes two single beds that match. The words after it give you the clue: beds, towns, brother, sister. Each one tells you which meaning is being used.
explain: «You get half your DNA from your mother and half from your father, but identical twins share the same DNA.» Here twin means people who are very alike because they come from the same egg. Read the whole sentence, not just the hard word, and the meaning will be clear.
fact: A twin is one of two children born to the same mother at the same time.
fact: Twin can also mean one of a pair of things that are the same or very alike, such as «twin beds».
fact: In British use, two towns are twinned when they are friends and partners with a town in another country.
fact: Identical twins come from one egg and share the same genes; non-identical twins come from two eggs.
fact: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
exercise: «One twin speaking for the other too much can leave the quiet one feeling invisible.» What is a twin in this sentence? | Two matching beds in one room | Two towns that are friends | A child who is one of two born at the same time | *A child who is one of two born at the same time to the same mother
exercise: Hotel signs say «twin beds». What does twin mean here? | A small, quiet room | Two towns that are partners | *Two matching single beds | A brother or sister
exercise: In British use, a town is twinned with a town in another country. What does twinned mean? | Fighting with a town in another country | Two towns that have the same name | *Friends and partners with a town in another country | A town that is very old
test: «Identical twins share the same DNA.» Which word tells you the twins are very alike? | *Identical | DNA | Share | Same
test: Which meaning of twin fits «twin brother»? | *One of two children born to the same mother at the same time | Two towns that are partners | Two single beds | A matching pair of socks
exam: What does twin mean in «twin towns»? | Two children born at the same time | A twin brother or sister | Two beds in one room | *Two towns that are friends and partners with a town in another country
